{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EEpd84NHt26JZydCnrwMgc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context and propose tasks for release 05.1 (expand, unexpand).\n\nFirst, let me understand the current state:\n- Release 05.1 has two use cases: rel05.1-uc001-expand and rel05.1-uc002-unexpand\n- Both have specstatus: spec_complete, codestatus: not started\n- The expand task (a9bc8aa) was already committed: \"Task 351: Implement cmd/expand (rel05.1-uc001-expand)\"\n\nWait, looking at the git history: `a9bc8aa Task 351: Implement cmd/expand (rel05.1-uc001-expand)` - this means expand is already implemented! So I should only propose unexpand.\n\n\nSince I'm limited to one task and expand is already done, I'll focus on proposing the unexpand implementation, which should follow the same pattern with its corresponding PRD and use case specifications. Now I'm ready to compose the task definition that the stitch agent will process.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27547,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27547},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27727d5c-f9ee-4030-807c-b494d7860a0b","uuid":"f76f159c-e4f3-45f3-b9b1-e19ca9b565ef"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EEpd84NHt26JZydCnrwMgc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test a spec-driven AI code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Specs in `docs/`, implementations in `cmd/`, shared libraries in `pkg/` (sys, format, testutils), build via `magefiles/`. Differential testing harness compares Go binary output against GNU reference byte-for-byte.\n\n**Current state:** Releases 00.0 through 05.0 have specs (some with code at v1 tags). Release 05.1 (tab conversion pair: expand, unexpand) is in progress — expand was just implemented (commit a9bc8aa). Unexpand remains.\n\n**Current release:** 05.1. One use case remains: `rel05.1-uc002-unexpand`.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nExpand is done. The only remaining work in 05.1 is `cmd/unexpand`. It follows the same pattern as expand (tab conversion) and depends on the same shared packages (pkg/sys for SIGPIPE, pkg/testutils for differential tests). No new library work needed.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Task: Implement cmd/unexpand (rel05.1-uc002-unexpand)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd016-unexpand.yaml (all requirements for unexpand)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.1-uc002-unexpand.yaml (use case flow and success criteria)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.1.yaml (test cases for unexpand)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared protocols: differential testing, SIGPIPE handling, graceful skip)\n      - cmd/expand/main.go (sibling utility for pattern reference -- expand converts tabs to spaces, unexpand is the inverse)\n      - cmd/expand/expand_test.go (differential test pattern reference)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests API)\n      - pkg/sys/signal.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler API)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/unexpand/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: unexpand implementation -- converts spaces to tabs\n      - path: cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gunexpand reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement the unexpand utility that converts leading blanks (spaces) to tabs,\n          reading from files or stdin. Default behavior converts only leading sequences of\n          blanks. With -a/--all, convert all sequences of two or more blanks at tab stops.\n          Match GNU unexpand behavior for all flags per the PRD.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Support --first-only (default behavior -- only convert leading blanks), -a/--all\n          (convert all suitable blank sequences), and -t/--tabs=N or --tabs=LIST for custom\n          tab stop positions. When -t is given, -a is implied. Match GNU unexpand flag\n          semantics exactly.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Handle multiple input files and stdin (when no files given or \"-\" is specified).\n          Process each line independently. Preserve trailing content after last tab stop.\n          Write to stdout. Exit 0 on success, exit non-zero on error with diagnostic to stderr.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests comparing the Go binary\n          against the Homebrew reference binary \"gunexpand\". Skip gracefully if gunexpand is\n          not in PATH (exec.LookPath + t.Skip). Set LC_ALL=C in test environment. Cover:\n          default (leading-only), -a flag, -t with single value, -t with comma-separated list,\n          stdin input, multiple files, lines with no blanks, lines with mixed tabs and spaces.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() per the shared protocol\n          in ARCHITECTURE.yaml. All cmd/ utilities that write to stdout must do this.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Use the same differential test pattern as cmd/expand: build binary with\n          testutils.BuildBinary, look up \"gunexpand\" via exec.LookPath, skip if not found,\n          define []testutils.DiffTest slice, call testutils.RunDiffTests.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Do NOT install any packages in the test or build. The reference binary \"gunexpand\"\n          must already be in PATH or the test skips gracefully.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Use flag or manual argument parsing consistent with cmd/expand. Support both\n          short (-a, -t) and long (--all, --first-only, --tabs) flag forms. Use --help\n          and --version following GNU conventions.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/unexpand/main.go compiles with no errors (go build ./cmd/unexpand/)\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go vet ./cmd/unexpand/ reports no issues\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Differential tests pass: go test ./cmd/unexpand/ -v (or skip cleanly if gunexpand not in PATH)\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Default mode converts only leading spaces to tabs at tab stop 8\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"-a flag converts all sequences of blanks at tab stops, not just leading\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"-t N sets tab stop width and implies -a; -t N1,N2,... sets explicit tab stop list\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: Reads from stdin when no files given or when \"-\" is specified\n      - id: AC8\n        text: Production code is under 250 lines\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27547,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27547},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27727d5c-f9ee-4030-807c-b494d7860a0b","uuid":"9e229153-5aec-433f-af2b-3be3dfa0f886"}
